    "alert_id": "ALERT_001",
    "title": "DTG-associated weight gain and metabolic deterioration",
    "message": "Guidelines note DTG is well-tolerated but hyperglycemia in non-diabetics has been reported. Patient gained 17kg (65→82kg, BMI 25.6→32.4) over 18 months on DTG, with new impaired fasting glucose (118 mg/dL), HbA1c 6.1%, dyslipidaemia (LDL 148, TG 212), acanthosis nigricans, and BP rise (118/74→138/88). She has ≥2 hyperglycemia risk factors: age ≥30, BMI ≥25, and family history of DM. Guidelines state clients with ≥2 risk factors need glucose monitoring every 3 months for 12 months after DTG initiation. Evidence for DTG attribution: temporal relationship with weight gain and metabolic changes after switch. Against: EFV may also cause dyslipidaemia; lifestyle factors unknown. No clinician plan was documented today.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Assess for DTG-related metabolic toxicity. Consider lifestyle intervention, weight management, and evaluate whether DTG continuation is appropriate given progressive metabolic syndrome. Document a formal plan.",
