  {
    "alert_id": "ALERT_002",
    "title": "Missing glucose monitoring per DTG risk-factor protocol",
    "message": "Guidelines require RBS/FBS every 3 months for the first 12 months in clients with ≥2 hyperglycemia risk factors on DTG. This patient had ≥3 risk factors (age ≥30, BMI ≥25, family history of DM) at DTG transition 18 months ago, but no prior glucose monitoring results are recorded. The first documented glucose (118 mg/dL) and HbA1c (6.1%) appear only now, well outside the recommended 3-monthly monitoring window. This represents a missed opportunity for early detection of DTG-associated hyperglycemia.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Establish ongoing glucose monitoring (FBS or HbA1c) at appropriate intervals. Screen for diabetes given current pre-diabetic range results and reinforce lifestyle counselling.",
